      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2004-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Writing \\(x = 100 - 2y,\\) the value of \\(x\\) is a positive integer precisely when \\(y\\) is a positive integer with \\(1 \\le y \\le 49.\\)\n\nThis gives \\(49\\) valid ordered pairs.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Solve for \\(x\\) in terms of \\(y\\)",
        "\\(x = 100 - 2y\\) must be positive, which bounds how large the positive integer \\(y\\) can be"
      ],
